 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "chagigah.24b.11",
   "daf": "24b",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "הָאוֹנֵן וּמְחוּסַּר כִּפּוּרִים כּוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא — כֵּיוָן דְּעַד הָאִידָּנָא הֲווֹ אֲסִירִי, אַצְרְכִינְהוּ רַבָּנַן טְבִילָה.",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: «An acute mourner and one who is lacking atonement» require immersion in order to eat sacrificial food, but this is not necessary for teruma. The Gemara explains: «What is the reason» for this decree? «Since until now it was prohibited» for «them» to partake of sacrificial food and they therefore might not have guarded themselves properly from impurity, «the Sages required them» to undergo «immersion» before eating sacrificial food."
  }
 ],
